# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUN-FOLDER ARTIFACTS — never repo files, at any path.
#
# The suite runs from a FLAT working folder (OPERATIONS §B, TESTING.md
# setup): sources at the root, every test and harness file together in
# one qa/. When that folder IS a clone, `git add .` sweeps the aliases
# and build products in with the real changes. That happened at v5.52 —
# the root DangerClose.jsx alias was committed, and because five suites
# (t8, t14, t16, t19, t22) read ../DangerClose.jsx, a committed copy
# would have let them run against a STALE source from a clean clone and
# report green. The missing-file error is the signal; these rules keep it.
#
# ⚠ Leading slashes are load-bearing: they pin each rule to the repo
# root so src/DangerClose.jsx stays tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/DangerClose.jsx
/v5*.jsx
qa/app_*.jsx
qa/app_*.mjs
qa/dom_bundle.cjs
qa/dom_v*.cjs
